course: dictionary
lesson: 2882
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. A doormat is a thick mat by a door where people wipe the mud off their shoes before they go in. «Wipe your feet on the doormat» is about this everyday meaning.
explain: Doormat has a second, informal meaning: a person who lets others treat them badly and never stands up for themselves. In a story about friends, «don't be a doormat» means stand up for yourself, but kindly.
explain: To find the right meaning, try each one in the sentence and see which fits. «Maya always says yes, even when she is treated unfairly. She is a doormat.» The first meaning makes no sense here, so the second must be right.
fact: A doormat is a thick mat by a door, where you wipe the mud off your shoes.
fact: Informal, a doormat is a person who lets others treat them badly.
fact: «Wipe your feet on the doormat» before you go into a home.
fact: Some people keep a spare key under the doormat, but this is not safe, because «burglars check under doormats».
fact: Standing up for yourself kindly means saying no politely, without being rude.
exercise: «Please wipe your feet on the doormat before you come in.» What is a doormat for? | *To wipe the mud off your shoes | To sit on while you read | To hold the door open | To keep a spare key safe
exercise: Leo says, «Don't be a doormat.» What does he mean? | *Do not let others treat you badly; stand up for yourself kindly | Stay on the mat all day | Wipe the mud off your friends | A mat that is too big for the door
exercise: Why is it not safe to keep a spare key under the doormat? | Because the key is too heavy to lift | Because keys get rusty in the rain | *Because burglars check under doormats | Because doormats are made of metal
test: «Maya always says yes, even when she is treated unfairly. She is a doormat.» What does doormat mean here? | A thick mat by the front door | A spare key under the mat | A wet, muddy shoe | *A person who lets others treat them badly
test: We wipe our shoes on the ___ before we go into the house. | *doormat | window | blanket | cushion
exam: Which sentence uses the informal meaning of doormat? | «The doormat is brown and new.» | «Wipe your feet on the doormat.» | *«Don't be a doormat; you can say no kindly.» | «Put the doormat by the back door.»
